<title>UK: KfW unit ups 10-year Eurobond to 350 billion lire.</title>
<headline>KfW unit ups 10-year Eurobond to 350 billion lire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 350 billion lire from 250 billion lire, joint lead managers Banque Nazionale del Lavoro, Banca Commerciale Italiana SpA and Bear Stearns said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The new paper has a 101.55 issue price.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> BORROWER   FW INTERNATIONAL FINANCE</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  KREDITANSTALT FUER WEIDERAUFBAU (AAA/AAA)</p>
<p> AMT    350 BLN LIRE  COUPON     7.25 PCT  MATURITY    16.JAN.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE *101.50    PAY DATE    16.JAN.97</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMS US/UK/IT/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *101.55 FOR 100 BLN LIRE INCREASE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
